1547..1618 Comment "/// Spinning a sum is composing the spins (cubical\'s `intLoop-hom`), by"
1619..1692 Comment "/// induction on the second summand. `spin` puts its new loop first where"
1693..1770 Comment "/// cubical\'s `intLoop` puts it last, so the law composes the spins the other"
1771..1837 Comment "/// way round, as the words compute: `Path.step(loop ∷ p, q)` is"
1838..1914 Comment "/// `loop ∷ Path.step(p, q)`. At zero `spin(Z)` is a call that returns the"
1915..1982 Comment "/// empty word, and the composite over it runs that call first; the"
1983..2047 Comment "/// composites the arms carry convert through their definitions."
