2317..2394 Comment "/// Winding a composite is summing the windings (cubical\'s `winding-hom`), by"
2395..2469 Comment "/// induction on the first loop, written last so its match stands directly"
2470..2548 Comment "/// under the recursion, where the checkers read it as a fold, and summed with"
2549..2613 Comment "/// `wind(q)` first because the sum descends its second summand:"
2614..2694 Comment "/// `Path.here(wind(q))` on the empty word, and the recursive call carried along"
2695..2768 Comment "/// `up` or `down`. The composite in its type is read off the parameters\'"
2769..2821 Comment "/// written types, and the kernel reads its endpoint"
2822..2874 Comment "/// `plus(wind(q), wind(p))` as the call it returns."
